Work Summary

Completed implementation of Section 24 of the MW–M31 merger analysis pipeline.
This section is designed to construct the full orbital timeline of the system
and identify key dynamical milestones such as pericentre passages, apocentres,
coalescence, and virialisation.

Note: The code has been fully written and structured but has NOT yet been run.
All results described below refer to expected functionality, not verified output.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Tasks Completed

- Implemented centre-of-mass (COM) tracking for both galaxies across all
  snapshots using existing pipeline utilities.

- Computed time-dependent separation d(t) and relative velocity v_rel(t)
  using finite-difference methods.

- Applied Savitzky–Golay smoothing to separation data to enable stable
  peak detection.

- Developed automated detection logic for:
  • Pericentre passages (local minima in separation)
  • Apocentre passages (local maxima)
  • Coalescence epoch (persistent threshold crossing)
  • Virialisation epoch (based on Jeans disequilibrium threshold)

- Built a structured event catalogue storing:
  • Snapshot index
  • Physical time
  • Separation distance
  • Relative velocity
  • Event type and ordering

- Implemented computation of dynamical quantities:
  • Specific orbital energy E_orb
  • Specific angular momentum L_orb

- Designed and coded full visualization suite for diagnostic outputs.

